# What the language bar should say
#
# MikroDash is a Go binary serving a TypeScript frontend, and GitHub measures
# everything in the tree except the one third-party file below.
#
# This file used to hide more. tools/ was marked vendored, and testdata/,
# internal/*/testdata/ and web/dist/ were marked generated, so GitHub left them
# out of the language bar. They are this project's own work (capture and
# generation utilities, recordings the tests replay, the built frontend), so
# since 2026-11-27 they are measured like the rest.
#
# The runtime image contains no node or npm binary and no JavaScript except the
# compiled frontend bundle, which is built from TypeScript.

# Genuinely third-party, vendored to avoid a CDN: Chart.js, self-hosted because
# this project serves no CDN assets.
web/public/vendor/** linguist-vendored
